    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m"{% if termsWithAnchors %} id="accessing-information" tabindex="-1"{% endif %}>Only access information you need for your job</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">Only search, access, view, use or share prisoner or a person on probation’s information when you have a legitimate work reason to do so.</p>
    <p class="govuk-body">Having access to a person’s prison or probation record does not mean you are authorised to view it.</p>
    <p class="govuk-body">Accessing information without a legitimate work-related reason is unauthorised access.</p>
    <p class="govuk-body">You must not:</p>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
      <li>browse or search records out of curiosity, including friends or family</li>
      <li>look up prisoners or people on probation unless you need to as part of your role</li>
      <li>access records at another establishment or information for someone else, unless you are authorised to do so as part of your work</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="govuk-body">Anything you do in HMPPS Digital Services must comply with the <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.cps.gov.uk/prosecution-guidance/computer-misuse-act" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Computer Misuse Act and other relevant data legislation</a>.</p>
    <p class="govuk-body">MOJ employees, contractors, consultants, and temporary staff must read <a class="govuk-link" href="https://justiceuk.sharepoint.com/sites/SecurityPolicyandGuidance/SitePages/Policy%20and%20Guidance/Asset%20Management/Acceptable-Use-Policy.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Acceptable use of IT policy.</a></p>

